 "step5_alternative_explanation": "The headline could be produced by (a) the identified rule's detail (write-through plus the asymmetric host refresh plus tail-first eviction) [the claimed mechanism], or (b) something much cruder that happens to agree: tier fullness alone, FIFO, or LRU without the host-path asymmetry. That is exactly what R2 tests, and the four comparison predictors share every line of the machinery except the policy switch, so a difference between them is the policy. A third alternative is that the streams are so lopsided (most arrivals cold at the small caps) that a predictor saying COLD always would score well; the per-class confusion matrices and the measured class mix are reported so that can be read off, and a constant-COLD baseline is included.",
